Z||000000||dodger||06-01-2000||07:12 PM||||My headlights shine on low beam only. When I switch to high beam they go off altogether, then on low again when I switch back. Also, the HIGH beam indicator light is on when they do shine. It started one night without warning when I turned them on. Anyone seen this?<P>Also...last night it wouldn't start for a few minutes...it would crank with zero catch...then started right up... The odd thing is it's been running great with zero rough running, and no problems at all today...it has: new dist.,plugs, spark plug wires, ignition module, fuel pump, egr tube, fuel sensor?,...I always use chevron mid-grade and lately used chevron injector cleaner... <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||06-02-2000||01:46 PM||||<BR>It is odd that both high beams do not work, but a similiar question has been posted within the last 1-2 weeks, if i remember correctly (try a search on headlights).<P>Try this link: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003844.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003844.html</A> <P>It may be that the high beams have blown within the headlight and the lights simply need to be replaced or there may be an electrical problem.<P>as for the slow start up, sounds like you replaced everything but the fuel filter, it may be giving you a problem.  Not sure which engine you have, so i am not sure how to help you further, but it sounds like a fuel delivery problem. so check your fuel filter first.<P>Added the Link<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||06-02-2000||02:38 PM||||Are you saying the high beam indicator stays on all the time the headlights are on?<P>If so, I would suspect a bad ground coming from the head lights (black wire).<P>Here's my theory: The indicator has a separate ground. If the headlights become ungrounded the high and low filaments effectively become series connected thru the shared ground terminal. The low beam current can flow thru <B>both</B> filaments and back thru the high beam indicator light to ground. The high beam current flows directly thru the indicator to ground (doesn't go thru the headlights at all). <P>Actually it seems with any Fiero elecrical problem the grounds are the first thing to check.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||dodger||06-02-2000||11:31 PM||||Thanks for the replies you guys. I wasn't very clear in my description. <P>The headlights work, but on low beam only: however, the HIGH beam indicator light is on at this time. <P>If I hit the high/low switch, the lights go out, and the high beam indicator goes out too.<P>This occured suddenly...no electrical work has been done lately...||||reg||1
